fear that. Could I be loved and accepted within this community? This shows us here, this is

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:13.470
actually what God wants. It's all of us. That's true for all of us. All of us have sinned and fall

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:17.850
short of the glory of God. All of us have run away from God. All of us have done things that we'd be

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:24.090
embarrassed if other people found out about, if not outright ashamed. And yet, the power of the

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:28.650
gospel here is that we can all be welcomed into the family of God. This is truly miraculous,

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.470
but it's also really, really important.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:34.130
Because when we think about that great commission

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.410
that Jesus has called us to,

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.050
to go make disciples of all nations,

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.590
well, how can we bring the gospel to others

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:42.090
if we are not living out that truth ourselves?

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.210
If we aren't just talking about it,

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.870
but living it in love and forgiveness and grace

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.410
and patience toward one another.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:50.810
And more than that, it's gonna be really hard

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:52.810
to take the gospel to the nations around us

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:54.850
if we can't even cross cultural boundaries

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.310
right here where we are.

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:58.930
and I think that also says something

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.470
to those in the world around us

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:01.650
who are kind of looking at us

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:03.950
and wondering what it is that we're about.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:05.890
I'll share a quick story with you here.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.270
This is from a long time ago

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.650
and I don't remember exactly when

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.230
but it's a long time ago in the history of our church

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:14.490
and we were doing some kind of outreach service activity

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:16.810
around the community here in Ann Arbor at the time.

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:19.970
We were like just serving some area,

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:21.550
I think a neighborhood here in Ann Arbor

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.630
and a bunch of us from our church were there

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:25.270
and were serving and just doing things

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.130
to help this community.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:30.270
and it was going really well. We were there, you know, for a good chunk of time, several hours,

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:35.030
and as it was getting toward the end of the event, somebody said something to me that I think really

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:39.390
stuck out to me. In order to understand this, I just want to briefly acknowledge something that

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:44.990
maybe not all of us realize, but I think it's just helpful, is our church is majority Pan-Asian.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:54.110
Okay, if you didn't see that yet, like, I didn't realize. Wait, what? No, okay, so we're majority

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:57.730
Pan-Asian right now, and we always have been. In fact, back at this time, we're even more so.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:03.210
Majority Pan-Asian ethnic groups within our church. And so we're there. We're all serving

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:07.530
in this community. And I was talking with one of the members of the community as we got to the end

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:11.210
of the day. We're finishing things up. And we were just talking. We were just chatting, talking

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:15.890
about life, getting to know each other. And then as we were talking, he just kind of looked out at

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:19.870
everybody who was serving and doing things. And he said something to me. He said,

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.210
man, those Asian folks sure are nice.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:25.920
I was like, okay.

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:28.980
But I kind of suffered.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:32.400
I was trying to figure out how do I sensitively say this.

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.480
I think I said something like,

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:36.160
they're not just Asian, they're Christian.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.740
Because I think what I realized happened there,

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.680
we wanted to be there to represent Christ.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:47.080
We wanted to be there to show the love of Christ

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.320
to our city, to this neighborhood.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:51.440
We wanted to be there to show people that God loves them.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:56.420
and that God has a purpose for them, and that Jesus came to save them.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:20:00.560
We wanted people to see Jesus, but what, at least for this man,

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:05.860
what he actually saw was just an ethnic group, a common ethnicity.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:09.720
And so what we wanted attributed to Christ,

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:13.040
he instead attributed to an ethnic group, a culture.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.260
And that stuck out to me at that moment.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:17.900
I mean, partly that made me feel a little weird.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:21.180
But, you know, as I thought about that,

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:27.080
I realized this is why actually this picture of the church we see in Antioch is really important.

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:30.440
You know, something else significant happened at Antioch.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:32.540
If you look in chapter 11, verse 26, it says,

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:35.280
In Antioch, the disciples were first called Christians.

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:38.500
And do you know why that happened?

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:43.040
It wasn't because they were just especially sincere in their faith more than anybody else.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:49.320
Prior to that time, anyone who was a follower of Jesus would have been called a Jewish follower of the way.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.860
That's what they would have been called, a follower of the way, a Jewish person.

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:59.540
But here now, for the first time, they couldn't peg this group as any one ethnic group.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:02.800
They couldn't say, oh, those are the Phoenicians over there.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.500
Oh, yeah, those are the Syrians over there.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.480
Oh, yeah, those are the Hittites over there.

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:09.480
Those are whoever.

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:12.380
They couldn't put it on any one ethnic group of people,

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:15.040
so they had to say, what's their common denominator?

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:16.480
What do they have in common?

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.540
Because it's not their ethnicity, it's not their culture,

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:19.800
it's not their background.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.380
Maybe it's not even their language.

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:22.600
Maybe it's not the way they dress.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:23.720
Maybe it's not anything else.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:26.980
The sole thing they had in common was that they were following Jesus.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:30.160
And so what can we do but call them Christian?

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:33.120
What can we do but identify them that way?

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.180
And I want to acknowledge as we look at this here

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:37.460
and think about what that means,

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:39.560
This is really hard.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:42.760
What we're talking about, being a transcultural spiritual family,

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.020
it's really, really hard.

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.160
It's not easy at all.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.800
But this, I think, is something that goes beyond demographics or statistics.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.960
It's not about those things.

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:56.060
At this level, it's about friendship.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:58.420
It's about trust.

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:00.720
It's about partnership.

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:03.620
It's about connecting with people at a deep level,

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:05.440
not just sitting side by side like this,

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:08.460
but really being in each other's lives and learning to trust one another.

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.780
And that's a really difficult thing to do.

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:13.800
And so that's why even I've been using that word transculture,

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:15.280
but let me just define it real quick.

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:18.120
The way we use that is to mean a decision to be uncomfortable

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:20.960
and cross cultural boundaries for the sake of the gospel.

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:23.160
That's what we mean when we use that word.

00:22:23.220 --> 00:22:24.660
It's not just about demographics.

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:26.760
It's a decision we make to say,

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:28.600
I'm not going to just stay in my comfort zone.

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:31.020
I'm going to go outside of that, beyond that,

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.760
to connect with someone who's different from myself for the sake of the gospel.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:37.720
And again, this is not our good idea as a church or something.

00:22:38.200 --> 00:22:40.660
Paul writes about this in 1 Corinthians 9.22.

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:45.180
He says, I have become all things to all people that by all means I might save some.

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:48.220
This is what we're trying to live out.

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:49.320
This is what we see happening.

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:52.300
This is what we want to live and be and breathe together.

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:54.080
And again, this is hard.

00:22:54.460 --> 00:22:57.700
Like, some of you, maybe you're curious about this and you want to dig into it a little bit more.

00:22:57.700 --> 00:23:02.280
Again, it's not just about, like, foods you eat or, like, different cultural things.

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:04.580
But, like, it gets to a lot of deep levels.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:07.220
If you want to look into it, there's a woman named Erin Meyer.

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:11.460
She actually studied this in a business context and wrote a book about it called The Culture Map.

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:15.420
And here's some different dimensions of culture that she talks about.

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:16.400
And we're not going to go through these.

00:23:16.460 --> 00:23:18.680
I just want to throw it up there just for us to think about.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:21.640
As you look at this and think about it, like, wow, okay.

00:23:21.940 --> 00:23:24.120
Like, there are so many different ways we can miss each other.

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:26.540
It can be anything from, like, very practical things.

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:29.700
Like, one person shows up on time because they see time as very precise.

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:34.420
To another person shows up, like, pretty late because they're like, oh, yeah, scheduling.

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:39.060
that's very flexible, that's very relational, I just show up, you know, whenever. We can miss each

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:43.300
other on these things, and it can get to very deep levels, and some of you may want to look into this

00:23:43.300 --> 00:23:47.820
a little bit more. She's talking about it in a business context, so she's not even getting into

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:52.640
things like how that affects our sense of social identity, or how we morally process things. There's

00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:57.280
much more than this that we can even miss each other on, and because of that, it's really, really

00:23:57.280 --> 00:24:01.800
difficult. And in fact, what I would want to let you know up front, if you're like, man, do I want

00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:06.920
to be part of this church? Do I want to be part of this kind of transcultural community? It's

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:11.580
really hard, and you'll probably experience things like frustration or disappointment or

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:16.320
discouragement. And I can share that even personally. Like today, there's still times I sometimes feel

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:21.420
like an outsider. I'm a lead pastor. And even when I first became a Christian, here within this

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:25.360
church, this is my only church I've ever been part of. And back my freshman year, when I came to know

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:29.560
Christ and joined this community, I was trying to get to know people, and I always had great

00:24:29.560 --> 00:24:33.400
relationships with older people in the church who really cared for me, took me under their wing,

00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:39.840
what I really struggled with was peer friendships. I really struggled with finding people my age,

00:24:39.920 --> 00:24:44.700
like my class, people who are like peers to me that I could be close friends with. It took a long

00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:49.580
time, and it was very frustrating and very difficult. Some of you may experience that.

00:24:50.040 --> 00:24:54.180
There are many times I actually wanted to leave and go somewhere else, but as I prayed through it,

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:59.480
I felt like God was calling me here because I felt these things were important. And so I struggled

00:24:59.480 --> 00:25:03.820
through that. And each of us is going to have to struggle through that in our own way. But the

00:25:03.820 --> 00:25:08.720
challenge here is if we want to reach the nations with the gospel, we need to learn to build those

00:25:08.720 --> 00:25:13.420
kinds of transcultural relationships. And I think in today's globally connected world, that becomes

00:25:13.420 --> 00:25:18.780
more important and more valuable than it ever has been before. So this is the kind of community that

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:22.740
we see in the church there in Antioch. And the third thing, last thing that we notice about this

00:25:22.740 --> 00:25:27.560
church is that they were led and empowered by the Holy Spirit. I noticed that in these few verses

00:25:27.560 --> 00:25:32.480
they're worshiping together, they're fasting together, they're praying together. And I think

00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:37.060
it's really interesting that this is actually where they're finding their unity. They're not

00:25:37.060 --> 00:25:43.220
finding their unity in something else, like, oh, we all happen to play soccer together, or we all

00:25:43.220 --> 00:25:47.980
happen to like this one kind of ethnic cuisine, or we all happen to wear the same kind of clothes,

00:25:48.080 --> 00:25:53.820
the same fashion. They're not finding their unity in anything else, but in that relationship with

00:25:53.820 --> 00:26:00.680
God. And I shared with you earlier that orchestra example, but here's maybe another one that ties

00:26:00.680 --> 00:26:05.880
into that same kind of thought a little bit, a quote from A.W. Tozer. He says, has it ever occurred

00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:12.360
to you that 100 pianos, all tuned to the same fork, are automatically tuned to each other? They are of

00:26:12.360 --> 00:26:18.040
one accord by being tuned, not to each other, but to another standard to which each one must

00:26:18.040 --> 00:26:20.020
individually bow. So 100

00:26:20.020 --> 00:26:22.080
worshipers met together, each

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:23.800
one looking away to Christ,

00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:25.980
are in heart nearer to each other

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:28.100
than they could possibly be

00:26:28.100 --> 00:26:29.900
were they to become unity conscious

00:26:29.900 --> 00:26:31.800
and turn their eyes away from God

00:26:31.800 --> 00:26:33.800
to strive for closer fellowship.

00:26:35.580 --> 00:26:36.160
You realize, I think

00:26:36.160 --> 00:26:37.800
this is what it comes down to.

00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:40.160
Being that transcultural spiritual family,

00:26:40.300 --> 00:26:41.860
it's not just shooting for demographic

00:26:41.860 --> 00:26:44.160
numbers or anything like that. It's really

00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:46.180
about saying we want to be united in

00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:52.240
Christ over anything else. Where do we find that? We find that as we worship together, as we pray

00:26:52.240 --> 00:26:57.380
side by side and for one another, as we hunger after God together, as we live out our faith and

00:26:57.380 --> 00:27:02.320
community focused on Christ, he brings us together. And that's what we see in this church.

00:27:02.440 --> 00:27:06.680
They're using their spiritual gifts to minister to each other. They're receiving guidance from

00:27:06.680 --> 00:27:12.120
the Holy Spirit. They're sending people out to reach the nations with the gospel. And notice

00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:17.160
that. This is really key as we kind of wrap up here today. Notice these couple things. Verse 3,

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:22.760
it says, after fasting and praying, they laid their hands on them and sent them off. They laid their

00:27:22.760 --> 00:27:27.040
hands on them and sent them off. If you just look one verse further, if you have your Bibles open,

00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:32.640
notice the beginning of verse 4. It says, so being sent out by the Holy Spirit. I don't know if you

00:27:32.640 --> 00:27:38.780
ever noticed that before. They laid their hands on them and sent them off. So being sent out by the

00:27:38.780 --> 00:27:44.100
Holy Spirit. Isn't that interesting? Which one is doing the sending? Who is it that's sending them

00:27:44.100 --> 00:27:49.720
out? Who is it that's sending out this team to go and bring the gospel to the nations? Well, I think

00:27:49.720 --> 00:27:55.400
what we see happening here is that actually what God is doing, the people are actually joining in.

00:27:56.020 --> 00:28:00.600
And this is important because I think for many of us, we ask the question, what does God want me to

00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:06.540
do? God, what do you want me to do? God, what's your will for my life? God, what do you want me

00:28:06.540 --> 00:28:11.340
to do? We ask that question, and it's not a bad question, but I think the better question to ask

00:28:11.340 --> 00:28:15.780
that maybe we can think about here is, God, what are you doing because I want to join you?

00:28:16.740 --> 00:28:21.600
God, what are you doing because I want to join what you're doing? Not God, what's your will for

00:28:21.600 --> 00:28:25.860
my life? God, what do you want me to do? But God, what are you doing because I want to join in what

00:28:25.860 --> 00:28:30.800
you're doing? And I think that's what's happening here. As the church, they're united in worship,

00:28:30.980 --> 00:28:36.520
in prayer, in seeking God. They realize the heart of God is to reach the nations, the Holy Spirit,

00:28:36.520 --> 00:28:40.640
is speaking to them, saying, I want you to send people out to go to the nations. It's what God

00:28:40.640 --> 00:28:46.340
is doing first. And then the people, they're joining in what it is that God is doing. And I

00:28:46.340 --> 00:28:52.080
share that because here today, we're sharing this vision of what I believe God is doing and wants

00:28:52.080 --> 00:28:56.880
to do within our church. That vision of becoming a transcultural spiritual family, reaching our

00:28:56.880 --> 00:29:01.240
neighbors, the nations, and the next generation. And if we think about that here today and say,

00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:02.900
God, what is it that you're doing?

00:29:02.980 --> 00:29:04.840
God, is this what you're doing?

00:29:05.620 --> 00:29:07.080
Then maybe that will lead us

00:29:07.080 --> 00:29:08.900
to recommit ourselves to this and say,

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:10.460
yes, God, we wanna do this together.

00:29:10.880 --> 00:29:12.600
Even when we talk about reaching our neighbors,

00:29:12.780 --> 00:29:14.160
the nations, the next generation,

00:29:14.500 --> 00:29:16.620
well, Jesus, you're calling us to be the salt

00:29:16.620 --> 00:29:19.200
and the light and love our neighbors as ourselves

00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:20.360
with people right around us.

00:29:20.380 --> 00:29:22.380
And those might be people that are very much like us.

00:29:22.840 --> 00:29:23.820
They might be people that are

00:29:23.820 --> 00:29:24.960
from the same ethnic background.

00:29:25.100 --> 00:29:26.940
They might be people who are studying the same major.

00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:28.880
They might be people who are in the same workplace

00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:29.760
or the same neighborhood

00:29:29.760 --> 00:29:31.360
or raising their kids in the same schools.

00:29:31.680 --> 00:29:32.620
Praise God for that.

00:29:33.280 --> 00:29:35.900
But also then we're challenged to reach the nations

00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:38.240
here in our campus and our city,

00:29:38.600 --> 00:29:41.900
here in this area where people come from around the world.

00:29:41.980 --> 00:29:43.160
Even if we go to the nations,

00:29:43.260 --> 00:29:44.580
we're called to be part of that.

00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:46.040
And Jesus has also called us

00:29:46.040 --> 00:29:48.220
to reach the next generation coming after us,

00:29:48.460 --> 00:29:50.740
whether that's kids or youth or college students

00:29:50.740 --> 00:29:51.760
or whoever that might be,

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:54.220
knowing there are new generations coming up after us

00:29:54.220 --> 00:29:56.140
that we are called to reach and disciple.

00:29:56.940 --> 00:29:58.260
And something I often think about

00:29:58.260 --> 00:30:03.220
is that here where we are, we have the privilege and opportunity to be part of God's mission

00:30:03.220 --> 00:30:09.600
in a way that many people in the world never get to be part of. I know right now believers who are

00:30:09.600 --> 00:30:13.980
living in Syria who have come to know Christ from a Muslim background and they have to live out their

00:30:13.980 --> 00:30:19.540
faith very secretly, very underground for fear of persecution against them. They don't never get to

00:30:19.540 --> 00:30:24.700
live out their faith the way that you and I do. I've met people deep in the Amazon jungle in Peru

00:30:24.700 --> 00:30:27.100
and they live in a village way back in the jungle

00:30:27.100 --> 00:30:29.180
and they will probably never see the outside world

00:30:29.180 --> 00:30:31.180
or maybe even see someone from another tribe.

00:30:31.500 --> 00:30:33.140
They will never get to live out their faith

00:30:33.140 --> 00:30:35.160
the way that we have the privilege to do.

00:30:35.580 --> 00:30:37.000
We are here in this place,

00:30:37.060 --> 00:30:38.900
on this campus in Ann Arbor, Michigan

00:30:38.900 --> 00:30:41.540
and we get to study and work and live

00:30:41.540 --> 00:30:43.720
and raise our families and hang out with people

00:30:43.720 --> 00:30:45.420
in a place where the nations gather

00:30:45.420 --> 00:30:47.160
and where the next generation comes

00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:48.400
to prepare for the future.

00:30:49.240 --> 00:30:51.480
And so as we start this new season of ministry

00:30:51.480 --> 00:30:53.480
this year ahead, let's commit together

00:30:53.480 --> 00:30:56.600
to becoming this kind of transcultural spiritual family

00:30:56.600 --> 00:30:59.120
and joining God in the work he is gathering,

00:30:59.280 --> 00:31:01.440
he is doing to gather all people to himself.

00:31:01.800 --> 00:31:03.920
That's what we want to do as we finish up this time.

00:31:04.380 --> 00:31:06.200
And a couple next steps I have for us here,

00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:08.520
because this can all be very just theoretical ideas.

00:31:08.820 --> 00:31:09.560
Can I give you some things

00:31:09.560 --> 00:31:11.080
that I hope will be a little bit more practical?

00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:13.880
We as a church will try to do different things together

00:31:13.880 --> 00:31:15.220
to live this out corporately

00:31:15.220 --> 00:31:17.420
in our gatherings and events and stuff like that.

00:31:17.740 --> 00:31:19.060
But a lot of this comes down

00:31:19.060 --> 00:31:22.140
to each one of us taking ownership of this calling

00:31:22.140 --> 00:31:23.440
and living it out together.

00:31:23.480 --> 00:31:24.940
And so what could that look like?

00:31:24.960 --> 00:31:26.380
The first thing I would encourage you with

00:31:26.380 --> 00:31:28.780
is practice living out the gospel in community.

00:31:29.460 --> 00:31:31.200
Practice living out the gospel in community.

00:31:31.460 --> 00:31:33.220
Again, we can't bring to somebody else

00:31:33.220 --> 00:31:35.680
what we are not living in and experiencing ourselves.

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:37.740
And this is what we really pray will happen

00:31:37.740 --> 00:31:39.140
within our life group communities,

00:31:39.400 --> 00:31:41.400
these biblical communities of grace and truth

00:31:41.400 --> 00:31:42.440
that we wanna belong in.

00:31:42.740 --> 00:31:44.260
And if you haven't signed up for a life group yet,

00:31:44.300 --> 00:31:45.700
you can do it with that link on the screen,

00:31:45.820 --> 00:31:47.340
hmcc.tech slash LG.

00:31:47.780 --> 00:31:49.200
We would love for you to get involved.

00:31:49.320 --> 00:31:50.900
And when you get involved in life group,

00:31:51.100 --> 00:31:52.900
it will not be a perfect community.

00:31:53.280 --> 00:31:55.000
Turn to someone next to you and say, it won't be perfect.

00:31:56.940 --> 00:32:01.320
When you join that community, it is quite possible, maybe even likely,

00:32:02.120 --> 00:32:05.040
that in that community, somebody might disappoint you.

00:32:06.320 --> 00:32:09.520
There might be somebody that you were hoping would come through for you in a certain way,

00:32:09.560 --> 00:32:10.460
and they might let you down.

00:32:11.140 --> 00:32:13.540
At the same time, you might be there in a life group meeting,

00:32:13.580 --> 00:32:15.720
and you realize, oh my gosh, I just said something,

00:32:16.300 --> 00:32:17.560
and it really offended that person.

00:32:17.560 --> 00:32:19.880
I didn't mean it, but I accidentally offended that person.

00:32:20.020 --> 00:32:20.980
Man, what am I going to do?

00:32:21.720 --> 00:32:23.440
Those things might happen in life group

00:32:23.440 --> 00:32:25.840
because we're people and that's what people do.

00:32:26.560 --> 00:32:28.920
But in that community, we are not without hope

00:32:28.920 --> 00:32:30.400
because in that community,

00:32:30.400 --> 00:32:32.420
we actually have the message of the gospel

00:32:32.420 --> 00:32:33.960
that we can share with each other

00:32:33.960 --> 00:32:36.120
that because Christ died on the cross for us,

00:32:36.360 --> 00:32:38.800
well, I can ask for forgiveness and I can be forgiven

00:32:38.800 --> 00:32:40.580
and I can offer forgiveness to others.

00:32:40.980 --> 00:32:42.420
We can live that out together

00:32:42.420 --> 00:32:44.300
and see that Christ is actually bigger

00:32:44.300 --> 00:32:46.300
than the ways we disappoint each other

00:32:46.300 --> 00:32:48.480
or offend each other or anything else like that.

00:32:48.540 --> 00:32:50.060
Let's learn to live that out together.

00:32:50.340 --> 00:32:51.840
Second thing I would encourage us with

00:32:51.840 --> 00:32:54.100
is to explore and celebrate other cultures.

00:32:54.600 --> 00:32:56.140
Explore and celebrate other cultures.

00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:57.900
This is something that I think it's really great

00:32:57.900 --> 00:32:58.840
just to be curious.

00:32:59.240 --> 00:33:00.760
And that might mean like asking someone,

00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:03.660
you know, what's something that you love about your culture?

00:33:04.260 --> 00:33:06.520
Ask that to somebody from a different cultural background

00:33:06.520 --> 00:33:06.840
than you are.

00:33:06.880 --> 00:33:08.620
What's something you love about your culture?

00:33:09.020 --> 00:33:11.080
And then maybe they'll share with you

00:33:11.080 --> 00:33:12.660
and you can share with them and you can learn

00:33:12.660 --> 00:33:14.660
and maybe even experience that together.

00:33:14.980 --> 00:33:16.000
I love that.

00:33:16.180 --> 00:33:17.940
Like, I mean, I think from my culture,

00:33:18.100 --> 00:33:19.160
there's something I grew up with

00:33:19.160 --> 00:33:23.360
is this Dutch pastry, because I'm half Dutch, and the other half, I'm not sure what I am, but I'm

00:33:23.360 --> 00:33:28.800
half Dutch. And there's this Dutch pastry called banquette. It's made with almond paste and like a

00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:34.600
nice flaky crust pastry. I love it. Everyone I've shared it with that is not like from a European

00:33:34.600 --> 00:33:39.700
ethnic background does not like it, okay? But I love it. But so then I look at our church, and I'm

00:33:39.700 --> 00:33:44.940
like, man, I love it because my ethnic background, we do not have a lot of flavor. We're not so good

00:33:44.940 --> 00:33:48.660
at that. And I'm like, man, praise God he put me in a church with some flavor. Let's share that

00:33:48.660 --> 00:33:50.800
flavor, okay? Like, let's

00:33:50.800 --> 00:33:52.720
enjoy that together, okay? And so this

00:33:52.720 --> 00:33:54.100
is where, like, share with each other.

00:33:54.440 --> 00:33:56.060
Share with each other. And

00:33:56.060 --> 00:33:58.500
let's be a community that celebrates

00:33:58.500 --> 00:33:59.980
that together rather than being, like,

00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:02.640
one thing I want to say, this means being transcultural

00:34:02.640 --> 00:34:04.620
as a church does not mean that we just sort of

00:34:04.620 --> 00:34:06.580
flatten all culture and become really bland.

00:34:07.660 --> 00:34:08.680
Okay? It means we, the

00:34:08.680 --> 00:34:10.500
cultures that are here, we celebrate.

00:34:11.120 --> 00:34:12.700
And maybe we do pay attention, like, man,

00:34:12.740 --> 00:34:14.740
if there's, like, a majority here and there's one person

00:34:14.740 --> 00:34:16.860
that's a little outsider, maybe we actually pay special

00:34:16.860 --> 00:34:18.620
attention to make sure that that person's culture

00:34:18.620 --> 00:34:24.100
also gets invited and celebrated and shared, but we want to lift up that celebration of different

00:34:24.100 --> 00:34:29.400
cultures, not try to flatten them all out, and just share that with those around you, and then lastly,

00:34:29.620 --> 00:34:34.180
the third thing is just discover your role in God's family. If you're here within our church

00:34:34.180 --> 00:34:38.760
community, I think it's because God has a purpose for you to be here, and for each of us, that's

00:34:38.760 --> 00:34:42.600
going to be different. We're going to talk about this some more next week and throughout the coming

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:47.220
year. I think God has a role and a purpose for each one of us, and for some of you, maybe you're

00:34:47.220 --> 00:34:51.560
the encourager that somebody else needs. For someone else, maybe you're the prayer warrior

00:34:51.560 --> 00:34:56.360
who goes into spiritual battle for the sake of others and for God's kingdom. Maybe you're the

00:34:56.360 --> 00:35:00.800
person that loves to serve. Maybe you're the person with the great listening ear. Maybe you're

00:35:00.800 --> 00:35:05.860
the person who loves to study and explain God's word. Maybe you're the person who loves to worship.

00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:10.920
All kinds of things. We need all of that. Just like that symphony we listened to earlier,

00:35:10.920 --> 00:35:17.420
every instrument, every voice, every section, all of it is all needed to become this kind of church

00:35:17.420 --> 00:35:22.800
that really displays the gospel to the world. So let's explore that, discover that, and then live

00:35:22.800 --> 00:35:27.260
that out together, because the body of Christ needs each one of us to discover our part and

00:35:27.260 --> 00:35:31.120
live that out in this family. Could you turn to somebody next to you and say, you're an important

00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:37.680
part of this family? Amen. We're going to spend some time in response here today. If I can invite

00:35:37.680 --> 00:35:49.920
us to stand together. As we stand here this morning, if you'll just bow your head with me

00:35:49.920 --> 00:35:59.600
for a moment. This is a, as we hear God's word and look into it together, we want to respond

00:35:59.600 --> 00:36:04.540
with prayer, with worship, saying, God, I don't just want to hear and go on my way. God, I want to

00:36:04.540 --> 00:36:09.780
build a relationship with you. I want to interact with you. I want to process with you the things

00:36:09.780 --> 00:36:14.860
that you're speaking to me about. And in this moment, just be here with the Lord for a moment.

00:36:17.010 --> 00:36:20.890
And even as we're just standing here, I don't know, maybe there's probably all different kinds

00:36:20.890 --> 00:36:25.770
the things going through all of our minds. Maybe for some of us, it's excitement. Maybe for some

00:36:25.770 --> 00:36:31.770
of us, it's anxiousness or fear. Maybe for some of us, it's just like, I want to go to lunch.

00:36:33.090 --> 00:36:37.770
And I don't know what it is for you. But in this moment, I believe God has a reason for each of us

00:36:37.770 --> 00:36:44.530
to be here this morning. And as we gather in this place and think about that vision, that calling that

00:36:44.530 --> 00:36:49.890
God has for our church that he wants to lead us into, I know what the Lord desires for us is

00:36:49.890 --> 00:36:56.670
actually not to focus on ourselves, but actually to focus on him. Because again, what all of this

00:36:56.670 --> 00:37:04.830
is about is not us trying to make something of ourselves, us trying to figure out all the details

00:37:04.830 --> 00:37:10.230
and all the dynamics of it. That's not what it's about. It's actually about focusing on God,

00:37:10.730 --> 00:37:17.010
trusting in Jesus, following the leading of his Holy Spirit, living that out in response to who

00:37:17.010 --> 00:37:23.610
God is and what he's done. And so here, whatever it is that's on your heart, maybe you feel like

00:37:23.610 --> 00:37:28.910
God is speaking to you about something specific today, meeting you in an area of discouragement or

00:37:28.910 --> 00:37:33.430
something that's got you down. Maybe it's excitement. Maybe it's like, God, I don't

00:37:33.430 --> 00:37:37.770
know. I'm confused. I don't know what to do. Can we bring those things to the Lord in this moment?

00:37:38.350 --> 00:37:43.930
And we want to bring those things to the Lord in worship. So again, that church in Antioch,

00:37:43.930 --> 00:37:50.330
they didn't find their unity, they didn't find their direction, they didn't find their purpose

00:37:50.330 --> 00:37:57.490
in focusing on themselves and what they could do. They found that unity in focusing on the Lord

00:37:57.490 --> 00:38:03.250
and looking up to who God is and reflecting on the gospel of Jesus Christ and hungering and thirsting

00:38:03.250 --> 00:38:07.850
after him together. So that's what we want to do as we begin this time of response. And the worship

00:38:07.850 --> 00:38:12.910
team is going to lead us in worship here together. And as we worship, if you want to just join in

00:38:12.910 --> 00:38:18.110
worship and be united in that together with all your heart, then do that. And if you feel like you

00:38:18.110 --> 00:38:22.190
need to just maybe spend some time to sit down and pray through something, go ahead and do that.

00:38:22.570 --> 00:38:26.850
But let's make this a time when we connect with God together as a spiritual family and invite

00:38:26.850 --> 00:38:31.810
him to do his work in us. So God, we invite you into this time as we meet with you, as we respond

00:38:31.810 --> 00:38:36.970
to you. Lord, we draw our hearts together with you in worship from all the different backgrounds

00:38:36.970 --> 00:38:41.790
represented in this room. Lord, build us up as this spiritual family. Even meet each of us in

00:38:41.790 --> 00:38:45.290
the personal things that you're speaking to us about and that we're struggling with,

00:38:45.390 --> 00:38:48.850
but draw every eye to yourself as we worship you together.
